<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western Chalukya Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/973">973</a>–<a href="/years/1189">1189</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Kalyani Chalukyas, Later Chalukyas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Western Chalukya Empire was a dynasty that ruled much of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 973 to 1189, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tailapa-ii">Tailapa II</a> after the fall of the Rashtrakutas and governing from Kalyani. It fought long wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a>, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi">Vikramaditya VI</a> it reached its height. Its feudatories, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a>, Seuna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadava">Yadavas</a> and Kakatiyas, divided its lands when it collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire.jpg" alt="Western Chalukya Empire" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikel3012 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Western_Chalukya_Empire_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
